WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.900
Speaker 1: Florida Governor Ron DeSantis&nbsp;
has pulled a disgusting political stunt&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:08.160
that actually isn't that terrible for some of&nbsp;
the people involved. And I'll explain that in a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:15.300
moment. But the big headline is that Ron DeSantis&nbsp;
flew 50 migrants to the swanky island of Martha's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:22.680
Vineyard. And this is really just a sick political&nbsp;
stunt. It's meant to trigger and own the libs and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:27.960
on and on and on. But I'm going to argue that this&nbsp;
is actually quite the opposite. A Business Insider&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:34.140
has a report about this. DeSantis sent 50 migrants&nbsp;
to Martha's Vineyard by plane as an anti-liberal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.140 --> 00:00:40.080
stunt. The locals pulled together to help&nbsp;
them. Now, I've spent a lot of time on Martha's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:45.720
Vineyard, and as soon as I saw the headlines, my&nbsp;
instinct was, I don't know that this is going to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:51.960
work out necessarily the way Ron DeSantis imagines&nbsp;
it working out, because Martha's Vineyard is very,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:57.480
very liberal, extraordinarily liberal. And it&nbsp;
only follows logically that you are going to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.480 --> 00:01:04.740
see the people of Martha's Vineyard come together&nbsp;
to help these 50 individuals. As the story goes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.740 --> 00:01:08.940
Governor, this is Business Insider. Governor Ron&nbsp;
DeSantis of Florida sent planeloads of migrants&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.940 --> 00:01:13.620
to Martha's Vineyard in Massachusetts. It was&nbsp;
apparently intended to shift some of the burden&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:20.100
of migration to a rich liberal area. Locals at&nbsp;
the exclusive destination where Barack Obama&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:26.820
owns property rallied to help out. State Senator&nbsp;
Julian Cyr of Massachusetts told The New York&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:32.700
Times about 50 migrants arrived in two planes&nbsp;
with no warning. Fox News Digital reported the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:36.600
story and had video of migrants disembarking&nbsp;
from planes. All right. You can imagine what it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:42.300
looks like for people to get off of a plane. Yes,&nbsp;
Florida can confirm the two planes with illegal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:46.980
immigrants that arrived in Martha's Vineyard&nbsp;
today were part of the state's relocation program&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:52.800
to transport illegal immigrants to sanctuary&nbsp;
destinations. That's Taryn Fenske, the comms&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:57.600
director for DeSantis. And then you just have to&nbsp;
look at the reaction from the island of Martha's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:02.880
Vineyard, Fernandez posting. Our island jumped&nbsp;
into action, putting together 50 beds, giving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:07.560
everyone a good meal, providing a play area for&nbsp;
the children, making sure people have the health&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:12.000
care and support they need. We are a community&nbsp;
that comes together to support immigrants.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:18.840
Another article from KBS, Florida's DeSantis flies&nbsp;
dozens of illegal immigrants to Martha's Vineyard,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:26.520
escalating tactic against, quote, sanctuary&nbsp;
destinations. Think about how absurd this is.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.520 --> 00:02:33.480
First of all, Florida spends a bunch of money to&nbsp;
fly people out. These folks appear to actually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:38.520
have come from Texas, not even from Florida. So&nbsp;
it's like, why is Ron DeSantis even involved? Why&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:43.560
is taxpayer money being spent to move people from&nbsp;
Texas to Massachusetts? That doesn't even make&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.560 --> 00:02:50.460
sense first and foremost. Secondly, from a fiscal&nbsp;
conservatism point of view, I think it would have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.460 --> 00:02:57.600
been cheaper for Florida to set up temporary&nbsp;
housing and vocational training for these folks,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.600 --> 00:03:04.200
eventually making them a productive, taxpaying&nbsp;
component of the Florida economy, rather than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:09.900
just blowing a few million dollars of taxpayer&nbsp;
money to fly people from Texas to Massachusetts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.900 --> 00:03:15.540
for a political stunt. And by the way, if these&nbsp;
folks eventually want to go back to Texas,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:20.280
they're going to be able to do it and nothing's&nbsp;
going to stop them. And Ron DeSantis isn't going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:26.940
to track them down and fly them out again. So&nbsp;
it's not only absurd, sort of superficially,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.660 --> 00:03:32.880
but it doesn't even make sense in terms of a&nbsp;
political stunt with taxpayer money now. In the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:38.820
meantime, the migrants are now in Martha's&nbsp;
Vineyard rather than Florida or Texas, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.820 --> 00:03:44.340
statistically, without casting any aspersions or&nbsp;
judgment, without making any moral statement. If&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.340 --> 00:03:50.880
you look at the HDI, that's the human development&nbsp;
index of Massachusetts, Florida and Texas,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.880 --> 00:03:55.620
which is a metric that considers a number of&nbsp;
different types of well-being. The migrants&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.620 --> 00:04:00.480
are certainly far better off in Massachusetts than&nbsp;
they would be in Florida or Texas, but that's sort&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.480 --> 00:04:08.460
of a different story. And then the last kind of&nbsp;
absurd or ironic component of this is that when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.460 --> 00:04:14.220
Ron DeSantis pulls these stunts and sends people&nbsp;
from red states to blue states, or when Abbott&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:18.780
Greg Abbott, the governor of Texas Republican,&nbsp;
has also pulled these types of stunts before.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.440 --> 00:04:26.100
Aren't you incentivizing immigration because&nbsp;
you're sending the signal to migrants undocumented&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.100 --> 00:04:30.720
immigration? That would be you're sending the&nbsp;
signal to migrants. Hey, listen, even if where&nbsp;&nbsp;

